stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Discovered : Candidate discovered via symbolic regression or HNN

    Discovered --> AnalyticalVetting : Enter validation gauntlet (WP4.1)

    note right of AnalyticalVetting
        Three tests:
        - Conservation: {I, H} = 0
        - Involution: {I, J} = 0
        - Independence: rank(∇I) = n
    end note

    AnalyticalVetting --> Rejected : Conservation test fails<br/>|{I,H}| > 10⁻¹²
    AnalyticalVetting --> Rejected : Involution test fails<br/>|{I,J}| > 10⁻¹⁰
    AnalyticalVetting --> Rejected : Independence test fails<br/>rank deficiency detected
    AnalyticalVetting --> MoralesRamisTest : All analytical tests pass

    note right of MoralesRamisTest
        Differential Galois Theory:
        - Phase I: Downstairs (reduced space)
        - Phase II: Upstairs (lifted space)
        - Kovacic algorithm
    end note

    MoralesRamisTest --> Rejected : Downstairs Galois group abelian<br/>(Unexpected - classical non-integrability not confirmed)
    MoralesRamisTest --> Rejected : Upstairs Galois group non-abelian<br/>(Non-integrable in lifted space)
    MoralesRamisTest --> MonteCarloValidation : Downstairs non-abelian AND<br/>Upstairs abelian (lift-integrability confirmed)

    note right of MonteCarloValidation
        Statistical validation:
        - 10⁴+ trajectories
        - Parameter space sweep
        - Mass ratios, energies, eccentricities
        - Chaos/regular stratification
    end note

    MonteCarloValidation --> Rejected : Statistical robustness < 95%<br/>(Not universal across parameter space)
    MonteCarloValidation --> Validated : Statistical robustness ≥ 95%<br/>(Robust across all tests)

    Validated --> Published : Manuscript submission (WP5)
    Validated --> Archived : Stored in validated integrals database

    Rejected --> [*]
    Published --> [*]
    Archived --> [*]

    note left of Validated
        Successfully passed:
        ✓ WP4.1: Analytical Vetting
        ✓ WP4.2: Morales-Ramis Test
        ✓ WP4.3: Monte Carlo Validation
    end note
